/*
  PDFRender - Windows BMP decoding.

  Covers what BMP files in the wild actually use: BITMAPCOREHEADER and
  BITMAPINFOHEADER (and the V4/V5 extensions, whose extra fields we
  skip), 1/4/8/16/24/32 bits per pixel, bottom-up and top-down, RLE4
  and RLE8, and BI_BITFIELDS masks.  Output is always XRGB32, one word
  per pixel, top row first - the same shape c/pdfpng produces.

